      "id": "ai-chips",
      "name": "AI chips up to the H200",
      "route": "US → China",
      "what": "Data center accelerators up to the H200's level: the A100 and H100, the cut-down A800, H800 and H20, the H200 and AMD's MI325X. Since 15 January 2026, license applications to export chips below 21,000 TPP and 6,500 GB/s of memory bandwidth from the United States to China or Macau are reviewed case by case. The exporter must certify, among other things, that US supply is sufficient and that a third party in the United States has tested the chips.",
