    {
      "id": "hbm",
      "name": "High-bandwidth memory",
      "route": "US → China, including HBM made abroad",
      "what": "Memory stacks with more than 2 GB per second of bandwidth per square millimeter, wherever they are made, including foreign stacks that the direct product rule brings under US control. The license requirement covers only Macau and Country Group D:5, the US list of arms-embargoed countries that includes China. For buyers in China or Macau, approval is presumed if they are headquartered elsewhere, and denial if they are headquartered there. License Exception HBM still lets an exporter in the US or in Country Group A:5, a group of close US partners, ship stacks below 3.3 GB per second per square millimeter without a license. The stacks must go directly to a packaging site for the designer that bought them.",
      "order": 5,
      "chapter": "memory-and-hbm",
      "initial": "open",
      "states": [
        {
          "date": "2024-12-31",
